# Example configuration for a foreground run (Node 20.6 or later):
#
#   cp bridge/example.env bridge/.env        # .env is git-ignored; never commit your ids
#   node --env-file=bridge/.env bridge/bridge.mjs
#
# Under launchd the same variables live in the plist (bridge/com.example.chat-bridge.plist).
# Paths must be absolute: neither Node's env file nor launchd expands ~ or $HOME.
# A variable already set in your shell wins over the same one in this file.
# Every value below is a placeholder.

# Required. The only directory the agent works in.
BRIDGE_WORKDIR=/Users/YOUR_USER/notes

# Required. The line `which -a claude` prints that starts with /.
CLAUDE_BIN=/Users/YOUR_USER/.local/bin/claude

# Required. Your own sender id under THIS bot app (scripts/whoami.sh prints it).
# Comma-separate several.
BRIDGE_ALLOWED_USERS=ou_xxx

# Optional. The bot's own id, for @-mentions in groups. Without it, groups are ignored.
# scripts/whoami.sh lists it among the mentioned ids when you @-mention the bot in a group.
# BRIDGE_BOT_ID=ou_xxx

# Optional. Ledger, sessions and heartbeat files. Default: ./state under the current folder.
# BRIDGE_STATE_DIR=/Users/YOUR_USER/Scripts/chat-bridge/state

# Optional. Default claude-sonnet-5.
# BRIDGE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Optional. Silence watchdog and hard cap, in milliseconds (defaults 5 and 45 minutes).
# BRIDGE_IDLE_MS=300000
# BRIDGE_HARD_CAP_MS=2700000

# Optional. Outside ping for a dead-man's-switch service. Off when unset.
# BRIDGE_HEARTBEAT_URL=https://example.invalid/ping/your-check-id

# Optional. A folder OUTSIDE BRIDGE_WORKDIR for the one carded action. Approval cards are
# off when unset.
# BRIDGE_OUTSIDE_DIR=/Users/YOUR_USER/Scripts/chat-bridge/approved

# lark-cli: its absolute path, and the profile of THIS bot app.
LARK_CLI=/usr/local/bin/lark-cli
LARK_PROFILE=your-bot-profile
